  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MANGROVE PROTECTION &amp; RESTORATION PN BAH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will: (1) Rehabilitate the hydrology of mangrove ecosystems in Salinas Bay and..Balandras Bay on Isla El Carmen, which will restore 600 hectares/1,482.61 acres, using an innovative..system of introducing seawater into the wetland and removing sediments that obstruct the tidal flow...(2) Repair 34 water gates and 10 km of levees in former salt evaporation ponds. (3) Protect the..restored wetlands and adjacent uplands through legal mechanisms: (3.a) In Salinas Bay, 590..hectares/1,457.9 acres of restored wetlands and 1,380 hectares/3,410 acres of uplands will be..protected through 20-year Conservation Agreements. (3.b) In Balandras Bay, 240 hectares/593 acres..of uplands will be protected through a 20-year conservation agreement. (4) Establish a baseline for..monitoring habitat and species. (5) With matching funds, build, equip and operate a biological station.</narrative>
  </description>
